+# Agent Note: Per-field model capacity provenance
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-28-model-capacity-provenance.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Model-listing endpoints may omit one or both capacity fields, installed catalogs can lag provider releases, and configured users may correct either field independently. Treating one row as a single-authority block either discards useful provider metadata or overwrites deliberate user values. Older settings also carry numeric capacities without provenance and must remain authoritative without a migration rewrite.
+
+## Decision
+
+Capacity resolution and persistence are independent for `contextWindow` and `maxTokens`. Each field follows `user` > `provider` > `official` > `estimated`: explicit or legacy user values survive refresh, provider metadata replaces only a missing or non-user field, the local official table supplies only exact verified IDs, and the estimate supplies the remaining gap. `contextWindowSource` and `maxTokensSource` carry the selected origin; discovery and its wire schema allow `provider`, `official`, or `estimated`, while persisted model configuration also accepts `user`. A legacy numeric field without its paired source is interpreted as `user` and is not rewritten merely by loading settings.
+
+The exact official table contains only `deepseek-v4-flash`, `deepseek-v4-pro`, and `deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp`, each with a 1,000,000-token context window and 384,000-token output limit. Unknown and near-match IDs use the conservative 262,144 / 32,768 estimate when the provider supplies neither field. This local correction table makes no additional capacity claim for another vendor or alias. The independent `llm-deepseek` adapter exposes 1,000,000 / 384,000 for those same three built-ins but retains its existing 1,000,000 / 256,000 fallback for an unlisted model ID.
+
+## Package ownership
+
+- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` owns the provider-neutral source union and optional discovery fields and preserves them when copying discovered rows.
+- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy` carries the optional fields through its API view and Zod wire validation.
+- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-pi-ai` owns exact-ID resolution, provider-listing normalization, configurable source fields, and legacy numeric compatibility.
+- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-settings-models` adopts discovery per field, preserves user-owned values, marks manual edits as `user`, clears a value with its source, and displays localized provenance labels.
+- `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-deepseek` publishes the verified capacities on its three listed DeepSeek V4 models without changing its unlisted fallback.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `pnpm exec vitest run packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/tests/capacity.spec.ts` passes 10/10 tests, including exact, near-match, mixed-provider, estimate, and prototype-key cases.
+- Focused discovery, core-copy, and API-schema suites pass 86/86 tests; their review coverage crosses the final discovery boundary and the Zod value schema.
+- `pnpm exec vitest run packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/tests/config.spec.ts packages/client/ui-settings-models/tests/provider-form.client.spec.tsx` passes 104/104 tests, including legacy ownership, per-field adoption/edit/clear behavior, omitted-source normalization, and localized labels.
+- `pnpm exec vitest run packages/llm/llm-deepseek/tests/adapter.spec.ts` passes 143/143 tests, including all three built-ins and the unchanged unlisted fallback.
+- Affected package no-emit checks, the settings client bundle, and the host library build pass.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+- **One source for the whole model row.** Rejected because a provider can disclose one capacity while the exact official table or estimate supplies the other; one label would misstate at least one field.
+- **Always replace configured values with fresh discovery.** Rejected because it would erase deliberate user corrections and reinterpret legacy numeric settings that previously behaved as authored configuration.
+- **Infer official capacity from provider names or model aliases.** Rejected because unverified aliases and third-party gateways can reuse similar names with different limits; only exact verified IDs can carry `official` provenance.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Configuration and wire formats gain optional provenance fields while old numeric-only settings remain valid and user-owned. Discovery becomes usable even when a listing omits capacity, but estimated values remain explicit guesses that a user or later provider response can replace. Maintaining separate pi-ai discovery estimates and `llm-deepseek` adapter fallbacks is intentional: they serve different entry paths and are documented separately so 32,768 and 256,000 are not mistaken for official DeepSeek V4 output limits.
