+# Agent Note: Ordered compaction summarizer fallback
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-08-28-compaction-fallback.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Automatic compaction can fail even when the conversation model remains usable: the configured or routed summarizer may exhaust capacity, hit a transient provider failure, or become unavailable. Retrying the conversation request does not provide a second summarization route, while routing every failure to another provider would forward private conversation history after cancellation, policy, or safety denial.
+
+The compaction transaction also permits only one durable checkpoint. A failed primary or fallback attempt must not leave partial summary content or a replacement that later attempts inherit.
+
+## Decision
+
+`BasicCompactionConfig.summarizationFallbacks` is an ordered global list of `{ provider, model, maxTokens? }` targets. The package default is an empty list, so existing consumers retain single-target behavior. The primary remains the explicitly configured summarizer or, when that pair is empty, the latest logged request target and then the agent target. A fallback entry without `maxTokens` inherits the resolved primary summarization cap; exact `modelPolicies` cannot replace the global list.
+
+The primary call and its configured retries settle before fallback routing starts. Operational failures, including capacity, rate-limit, timeout, and provider failures, are eligible. Abort or cancellation, shutdown, policy, safety, and content-filter signals deny fallback. A fallback missing a valid credential or adapter route, or naming an unresolved provider/model, stops the chain so later targets cannot bypass deployment intent. The same signal reaches every attempt, and cancellation checked between attempts remains authoritative.
+
+Every target receives the same replayed system prompt, tool schemas, shadowed messages, and final compaction instruction. A successful fallback therefore produces the same safe-text validation result as the primary. The region transaction commits no summary or replacement for failed attempts; after one target succeeds it appends exactly one `compaction/summary` and one adjacent replacement, and the summary records the winning provider, model, cap, output, and usage.
+
+### Migration considerations
+
+Omitting `summarizationFallbacks` preserves the prior behavior. A deployment opts in by adding the ordered list at the top-level compaction policy; route-specific policy entries continue to select primary limits but do not create separate fallback chains. The Agent Pi default target is `deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp` with `maxTokens: 32768`; the package itself does not silently add that route.
+
+Selecting a different provider forwards the replayed conversation across that provider's privacy and data-handling boundary and can incur an additional model charge. Deployments must provision and authorize every target before enabling it.
+
+### Keyless evidence
+
+The assembled headless compaction-recovery snapshot uses `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-replay`. Its sidecar makes the primary summarizer fail with `CONTEXT_WINDOW_EXCEEDED`, then supplies a deterministic complete response for `deepseek-official/deepseek-v4-flash-vision-exp`. Full sidecar consumption proves the failed call and fallback call both occurred without a credential or network request. The persisted and stream snapshots contain one fallback-provenance `compaction/summary`, one replacement, and no primary partial summary before the original turn resumes with `COMPACTION RECOVERED`.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Leave fallback to adapter retries.** Adapter retries stay within one provider/model route and cannot express an ordered deployment-level route change or attach the winning target's provenance to the compaction transaction.
+
+**Fallback after every failure.** Rejected because cancellation, shutdown, policy, safety, and content-filter outcomes are authority decisions, not availability failures. Crossing providers after any of them would bypass the decision and disclose the replayed conversation.
+
+**Commit each attempt as a partial summary.** Rejected because later attempts would inherit untrusted or incomplete model output and consumers could observe more than one checkpoint. Failed attempts remain call failures; only the winner reaches the durable summary and replacement pair.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `pnpm run test:snapshot -- examples/headless-agent/tests/headless.snapshot.ts -t "recovers from context overflow through an assembled compaction"`
+- `pnpm exec vitest run packages/compaction/compaction-basic/tests/config.spec.ts packages/compaction/compaction-basic/tests/fallback.spec.ts packages/compaction/compaction-basic/tests/compaction-basic.spec.ts -t fallback`
+- `pnpm run verify-agent-note-format`
+- `pnpm run verify-md-wrap && pnpm run verify-md-links && pnpm run verify-package-readme-model-experience && pnpm run verify-package-readme-limitations`
+
+## Consequences
+
+Compaction survives eligible primary failures when an authorized target succeeds, while denial and cancellation remain authoritative. Existing configurations do not change unless they add a fallback list. Successful snapshots and consumers see one atomic checkpoint with truthful winning-target provenance.
+
+Fallback resilience spends another model call and may move private history to another provider. Missing fallback deployment prerequisites fail the transaction instead of silently skipping to a later route, and diagnostics retain sanitized target/outcome facts without provider response text.
